--
-- Test Description
-- This test checks the operation of the TX DMA wrapping when collisions
-- occur at various times during the wrapping frames.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- * Checks the TX queue pointer operation during wrapping.
-- * Checks that collision retries occur from the correct queue locations.
-- * Checks that the wrapping operation is unaffected by collisions.
-- * Checks that used bits read after the collided frame do not affect it.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--
--  3. Try various combinations of multi and single buffer frames, that
--     wrap at various points within the frame and experience collisions
--     on different buffers.
--
-- TEST 1:
-- Try a collision on the fifth buffer of a six buffer frame that wraps
-- after the third buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 2:
-- Try a collision on the fourth buffer of a six buffer frame that wraps
-- after the third buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 3:
-- Try a collision on the third buffer of a six buffer frame that wraps
-- after the third buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 4:
-- Try a collision on the third buffer of a six-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the first buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 5:
-- Try a collision on the second buffer of a six-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the first buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 6:
-- Try a collision on the first buffer of a six-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the first buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps.
--
-- TEST 7:
-- Try a collision on the only buffer of a single-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the only buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps and then subsequently transmits another
-- good multi-buffer frame.
--
-- TEST 8:
-- Try a collision on the only buffer of a single-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the only buffer. This time delay the collision such that the second
-- frame is starting to be fetched.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps and then subsequently transmits another
-- good multi-buffer frame.
--
-- TEST 9:
-- Try a collision on the only buffer of a single-buffer frame which wraps 
-- after the only buffer.
-- Check that retry starts at beginning again and successfully transmits the
-- frame and that the queue still wraps but then reads a used bit.
--
--
--  4. Check statistics for above operations.
--
-- ************************************************************************** --



--******************************************************************************
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--******************************************************************************
wait_states     0
bus_grant_delay 2



--******************************************************************************
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts and then enable 
--     transmit in 100M half duplex mode from a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--******************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbwr      04 00080000  -- enable 100M mode into 32-bit bus




